   "aliases": [],
   "tags": [],
   "answer": "Every Sportradar Media API will include a for every endpoint. Use this tool to configure requests and browse the data inside the **Response** section. <img src=\"https://files.readme.io/507d16d-image.png\" style={{ display: 'block', margin: 'auto', border: '1px solid black' }} /> <img src=\"https://files.readme.io/6d7adb3-image.png\" style={{ display: 'block', margin: 'auto', border: '1px solid black' }} /> Path parameters will include all valid enums for a given field, when applicable. In this example, we provide all valid languages returned for an endpoint. <img src=\"https://files.readme.io/947033a-image.png\" style={{ display: 'block', margin: 'auto', border: '1px solid black', width: '500px' }} /> Some parameters (such as `game_id` in the below sample) will require a unique identifier. Locate valid game, team, and player Ids in separate API endpoints. <img src=\"https://files.readme.io/1bea188-image.png\" style={{ display: 'block', margin: 'auto', border: '1px solid black', width: '500px' }} /> For any issues in creating working requests, ensure that: * Your API key is included in the **Header** text bar within the **Credentials** section. * All parameters in your request are valid.",
