   "aliases": [],
   "tags": [],
   "answer": "Use the `id` for your selected game to start a session. At this point the specific feed—if multiple feeds are available—is not needed. ```curl curl --location --request POST 'https://playback.sportradar.com/graphql' \\ --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\ --data-raw '{ \"query\":\"mutation CreateSession($input: CreateSessionInput!) { createSession(input: $input) }\", \"variables\":{ \"input\":{ \"recordingId\":\"95aa13a0-6538-11ef-9287-d597687b4672\" } } }' ``` This request uses `recordingId\":\"95aa13a0-6538-11ef-9287-d597687b4672` in the above NFL response sample. The response returns your unique `sessionId` to be used in subsequent data API requests. ***",
   "product": "API Betting",
   "entities": [
    "API Betting"
   ],
   "source": "docs",
