   "id": "docs-tutorials-android-native-integration-prerequisites",
   "question": "Android Native Integration for Web Widgets — Prerequisites",
   "aliases": [],
   "tags": [],
   "answer": "Before starting, ensure you have: Android Studio with Compose and WebView available Client ID - see how to obtain one Basic widget integration experience - completed the Getting Started guide Familiarity with the SIR API (addWidget, updateWidget, setClientTheme, and related methods) A valid match ID (or other entity ID) for testing For the message bridge shown below, add the Jetpack WebKit dependency: [versions] androidxWebkit = \"1.16.0\" [libraries] androidx-webkit-webkit = { module = \"androidx.webkit:webkit\", version.ref = \"androidxWebkit\" } implementation(local.androidx.webkit.webkit) Overview: The generic integration flow is: Build the shared Android host: Create a reusable WebView host with a message bridge, height observer, and optional JavaScript access. Build the widget HTML page: Follow the Sportradar JS widget docs for the widgetloader bootstrap and SIR(\"addWidget\", ...) call. Host the page in Compose: Load the HTML with loadDataWithBaseURL(...) and size the WebView from reported content height. Handle events and live updates (optional): Receive widget callbacks through SportradarWidgetsSDK, and optionally call SIR(...) from Android without reloading.",
   "product": null,
   "entities": [],
