   "question": "iOS Native Integration for Web Widgets — What to implement",
   "aliases": [],
   "tags": [],
   "answer": "The following pieces are enough for an iOS integration: The shared SwiftUI host web view: SportradarWidgetView Widget HTML built according to Sportradar’s JS documentation Handling of onMessage for height and widget callbacks Optionally onBridgeReady / SrJavaScriptBridge for Swift → JS You may choose to add code that builds widget HTML from parameters or automatically injects the Sportradar loader bootstrap. Those helpers are useful, but they are not required for a basic implementation. Generic vs widget-specific: Shared across all widgets: SportradarWidgetView / SrJavaScriptBridge srBridge message handling Height reporting and native frame sizing Base URL loading behavior Changes per widget: Widget name Props Loader options Optional callbacks How you store or generate the HTML is an app concern, not part of the host.",
