   "id": "docs-tutorials-ios-native-integration-step-2-implement-a-message-handler-and-js-swift-communication",
   "question": "iOS Native Integration for Web Widgets — Step 2: Implement a message handler and JS → Swift communication",
   "aliases": [],
   "tags": [],
   "answer": "Register a WKScriptMessageHandler so JavaScript can post into Swift via window.webkit.messageHandlers.srBridge. Swift forwards each payload to an onMessage closure. This guide chooses: the handler name \"srBridge\" a type key on every payload, with branching on type in onMessage a single message handler for all JS → Swift traffic (height in Step 3; widget callbacks in Step 7), to keep the example small Extend the Step 1 host: Make Coordinator conform to WKScriptMessageHandler Register the handler on WKUserContentController in makeUIView Forward message.body to an onMessage closure Remove the handler in dismantleUIView to avoid retain leaks struct SportradarWidgetView: UIViewRepresentable { static let messageHandlerName = \"srBridge\" let html: String let disableScroll: Bool var onMessage: ((Any) -> Void)? private static let baseURL = URL(string: \"https://widgets.sir.sportradar.com/\")! init( html: String, disableScroll: Bool = false, onMessage: ((Any) -> Void)?",
   "product": null,
   "entities": [],
   "source": "docs",
   "pageTitle": "iOS Native Integration for Web Widgets",
   "heading": "Step 2: Implement a message handler and JS → Swift communication",
