   "id": "docs-troubleshooting-error-handling-what-is-widget-error-handling",
   "question": "What Is Widget Error Handling?",
   "aliases": [],
   "tags": [],
   "answer": "Widget allows you to gracefully manage situations where widgets encounter problems during loading or runtime. With proper error handling, you can: Prevent poor user experience - Hide or replace widgets that fail to load instead of showing error messages Maintain page integrity - Keep your page layout clean even when widgets encounter issues Provide fallback content - Display alternative content when widgets are unavailable Debug integration issues - Identify and resolve configuration problems during development The system provides multiple approaches: silent mode for production environments, the onTrack callback for custom logic, and visual error indicators for development and debugging.",
   "product": null,
   "entities": [],
   "source": "docs",
   "pageTitle": "Error Handling",
   "heading": "What Is Widget Error Handling?",
   "headingLevel": 2,
   "site": "apidocs.sportradar.com",
