   "question": "JSON Web Token (JWT) — Step 4: Pass JWT to Widgets",
   "aliases": [],
   "tags": [],
   "answer": "Deliver the signed JWT from your backend to your frontend application, then pass it to the widget during initialization. SIR Integration Complete Frontend Example Pass the JWT as a property when adding the widget using SIR: SIR(\"addWidget\", \"#my-widget\", \"widget_name_here\", { jwt: generatedJwtToken, // ... other widget properties }); Key Rotation: Rotate signing keys without service interruption: Generate a New Key Pair: Create a new RSA key pair using the same process as Step 1. Submit the Public Key: Send the new public key to your Sportradar representative. Wait for Confirmation: Sportradar adds the new key to your configuration and notifies you. Both old and new keys work during the transition. Switch Your Backend: Start signing with the new private key, then inform Sportradar when migration is complete so the old public key can be removed.",
