   "id": "docs-examples-adapter-tickets-endpoint-example-betslip-response-format",
   "question": "Implementing the Tickets Adapter Endpoint — BetSlip Response Format",
   "aliases": [],
   "tags": [],
   "answer": "The response must conform to the BetShareResponse type: { bets: BetSlip[] } Property Type Description id string Unique identifier for the bet (required) betSlipId Optional secondary identifier for client-side matching betType Bet type (e.g., \"single\", \"multibet\") currency Currency code (e.g., \"USD\") combinedOdds { decimalValue: number; displayValue: string } Combined odds for the bet stake { value: string } Stake amount as a string payout Potential payout as a string cashOut Cash out value as a string bets Bet[] Array of bets within the slip (market, outcome, event details) The response object must include the bets property and not include a tickets property. The BetShareResponse type explicitly excludes tickets (defined as tickets?: never).",
   "product": null,
